**Implication:** `ADJACENCY_TO_ONE_CUBIC` states \(1-A_{ADJ}(r)=O(r^3)\), which for
small \(r\) gives \(A_{ADJ}(r)\ge1-Cr^3\ge\tfrac12\) — the small-r half of
`ADJ_POSITIVITY_UNIFORM` for free. Only the compact remainder
\(r\in[r_1,0.025]\) then needs GP-DER-008's argument. The two OPEN nodes are
sequential, not parallel; the registry should record the implication so nobody
works the small-r positivity separately.

**Sources:** `ADJACENCY_TO_ONE_CUBIC` currently cites only measured diagnostics
(GP-AUD-017, GP-DATA-020). The analytic route exists and should be cited:
AO48-DER-005 §2 (the cubic-level \(r^3\) law is exact-asymptotic given compact
s-support of the failure set) and AO48-DER-007 §5 (the boundary-layer inclusion
sketch that supplies the compact support deterministically). Corresponding
falsifier to add: *one recorded escape below its per-sample step-(i) threshold* —
runnable on existing ensembles in one pass, already pre-committed in DER-007 §5.

