# §4. Verifier code audit (GP-DATA-022)

**Hand-trace of the 8 negative tests: all PASS as claimed.** Each mutation
produces its required needle through the traced control flow (e.g., test 2 empties
`bridge_ids` while leaving `dependency_ids` intact, so exactly `MISSING_ADJ_BRIDGE`
fires; test 7's "NONEXISTENT" fails both membership checks). Status:
CONFIRMED-BY-HAND-TRACE — I cannot execute, and a hand trace is weaker than a run;
anyone with a runtime should still execute the receipt.

**Hole 1 — cycles validate silently.** `closure()` detects a cycle and returns the
sentinel `{"cycle"}` — which flows into `blockers` and suppresses promotion, but
**appends no error**: `report["valid"]` stays `True` for a machine whose proof
graph is circular. A registry whose worst failure mode — circular justification —
passes validation is under-defended. Proposed **negative test 9**: mutate
`TYPED_REGIONAL_DEFECT_CUBIC.dependency_ids = ["Q_TYPED_MS_RATE"]` (creating a
2-cycle through the existing edge) and require a `CYCLE` error; implement by
appending `f"{cid}:CYCLE"` when the sentinel is generated.

**Hole 2 — `P_ADJ-CANDIDATE` escapes the P_ADJ checks.** The bridge/mark
enforcement fires on `measure_tag == "P_ADJ"` (equality), so
`THEOREM_B_ADJ_CONTACT_FACTOR` under `P_ADJ-CANDIDATE` is never checked for the
bridge — and indeed carries `bridge_ids: []` today. Fix: `startswith("P_ADJ")`.
Proposed **negative test 10**: strip `GRADIENT_ADJACENCY_MS` from
`THEOREM_B_ADJ_CONTACT_FACTOR` and require `MISSING_ADJ_MARK` under the prefixed
check.

**(c) Object-dependency smuggling.** `closure()` recurses only into deps that are
*claims*; deps that are objects contribute no status. Any claim can therefore
lower its apparent blocker set by depending on an object rather than on the claim
about that object — §2(c) is a live instance. Fix options: require
`dependency_ids` ⊆ claims (objects belong in `required_marks`/`law_object`), or
recurse a declared `claim_for` pointer on objects.

**(d) Nit.** The bare-object guard `obj in {"Q","q","Q0",""} and is_q_claim(c)`
lets a literal `Q0` law_object through when the statement avoids "Q_" — harmless
today only because `UNKNOWN_OBJECT` fires anyway; dropping the conjunct makes the
intent unconditional.

