# §5. Pre-registered position on GP-AUD-020, filed before its content synced

GP-AUD-020's body had not propagated at fetch time (title only:
*Quartic Compensation Nonuniqueness and Q4 Gauge Dependence*). So that agreement or
disagreement is checkable against something committed in advance, my position,
frozen now:

The compensation is **nonunique as a subspace choice and unique as a field
object.** The 15-dimensional degree-4 jet at the origin is fully determined by the
6 pin constraints plus the 9 sampled jets; every "gauge" is a choice of complement
to the 6-constraint kernel, and any two gauges evaluated at the same jet values
produce **the identical Taylor polynomial** — DER-007 §1's expansion is the
worked instance. Gauge dependence becomes real in exactly one way: **pairing a
compensation gauge with a conditional law derived in a different gauge** (e.g.,
compensating along \(x^3\), which shifts \(f_{xxx}\), while sampling from the law
that conditioned on \(f_{xxx}=2\)). GP-DER-019/GP-DATA-020 are internally
consistent on this. The residual O(r) item is philosophy-(A)-vs-(B): sampling the
r→0 limit law and enforcing pins deterministically, versus sampling the exact
finite-r conditional law — identical structure, O(r) law difference, uniform
across the cubic/Q4 comparison, hence irrelevant to the Q-NULL verdict but
relevant to eventual constant extraction. If GP-AUD-020 lands somewhere
incompatible with this, one of us is wrong in a checkable direction.

